\begin{abst}
 Thanks to Berkovich's presentation of $p$-adic analytic geometry, it is
 possible to make sense of the familiar monodromy principle in the
 exotic world of $p$-adic manifolds. Its application is however more
 limited than in the classical case, because (1) sheaves of solutions of
 linear differential equations 
